# Upper cervical attachment reasoning — draft

Four original reasoning prompts distinguish the paired C1–occiput muscles by attachment and listed head action. They use the eight single-file, exact source identities in `content/upper-cervical-reasoning-pins.json` at parent source `0327b6360e18b62563265d115df2b779c9397792`. The code checks the complete pinned `BodyStructure` identity through `sourceCanonical`, including source-file hashes, rather than accepting a name or FMA match alone.

