## Reference purpose and limits

- [UAMS muscles of the back region](https://medicine.uams.edu/neuroscience/education/medical-school-courses/human-structure-module/anatomy-tables/muscle-tables/muscles-of-the-back-region/) supports the posterior minor and superior oblique attachments, extension, and superior oblique's suboccipital triangle boundary.
- [Texas Tech muscles of the head and neck](https://anatomy.ttuhscep.edu/anatomytables/muscles_head_neck.html) supports anterior and lateral rectus capitis attachments, head flexion and lateral bending respectively.

The prompts and explanations are new MIT project text. No reference tables, questions, images, diagrams, or other media are redistributed. Existing source-mesh credit and licence policy remains unchanged. Mesh selection does not prove dynamic motion, CT/MRI visibility, registration, or patient-specific function. This is revision 1 with `draft` readiness; no clinical or radiologist approval is asserted. Revision-bound radiologist sign-off remains required.
